# <name> — coding standards

The rules this repo's code follows. Mandatory context, named by [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

## Baseline

The MinionsFactory `mf-build` skill's rules apply as written: comments `C1`…`C12`, tests `T1`…`T6`, prose
`P1`…`P13`. Formatter and linter settings stay in their own config files.

## The gate, per stack

**Any stack:** the gate runs one tool per job — format, lint, types, tests with coverage, security patterns — and
`docs/decisions.md` records each choice. The gate's secret scan, `betterleaks dir . --no-banner --redact`, stays,
and reads what git can track: a path `.gitignore` gains joins `.betterleaks.toml`'s allowlist.

| stack | the gate adds |
|---|---|
| Python | Ruff with `B` and `S` · ty · deptry · pytest with `--strict-markers` · diff-cover on coverage's XML |
| TypeScript | `tsc --noEmit`, or `vue-tsc --noEmit` · Oxlint · knip · vitest with coverage · diff-cover on its lcov |
| Docker | Hadolint |

**Slow tests:** a test over 5 s carries a `slow` marker, and `make check` runs the gate's fast steps without them.
The build runs `make check` after each phase but the last, and the gate after the last.

